<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maximilian II Emanuel, Elector of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1662">1662</a>–1726</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Max Emanuel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Max Emanuel was Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> from 1679 to 1726. He won fame fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, storming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> in 1688, and governed the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> from 1692. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a> he allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, lost Bavaria after the defeat at Blenheim in 1704 and went into exile, regaining his lands only in 1714.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maximilian-ii-emanuel-elector-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Maximilian II Emanuel, Elector of Bavaria" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andreas Møller · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%B6ller_-_Maximilian_II_Emanuel_of_Bavaria_-_Torre_Abbey.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
